    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14423" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dissŏlūbĭlis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		dissolvo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that may be dissolved</i>, <i>dissoluble</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mortale omne animal et dissolubile et dividuum
					sit necesse est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 3, 12, 29</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coagmentatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 8, 20</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Lact. 2, 8, 39</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 8,
			10</span></i>.— <i>Comp.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mutabilius et dissolubilius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug. de Genes. 8</span></i>
			.</div>
